ns, and has 108 smaller shrines inside its compound. It remains in active worship, with Parvati honoured as Annapurna.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":2.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Lingaraja Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kalinga (Deula style)","construction_century":null},{"id":"6b28ecc6-fe63-4384-bfbc-81d54fb72b10","name":"Puruhutika Devi Temple, Pithapuram","deity":"Puruhutika (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Kakinada","town":"Pithapuram","latitude":17.1068,"longitude":82.2433,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Godavari","river_distance_km":2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:10:03.827717+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A small shrine in the north-east corner of the Sri Kukkuteswara Swamy Temple complex, one of the Ashtadasha (18) Shakti Peethas. The goddess is worshipped as Puruhutika — \"she worshipped by Puruhuta (Indra)\" — depicted with four arms holding a seed-bag, an axe, a lotus, and a honey-vessel. Within the same temple grounds is Pada Gaya Sarovaram, a sacred tank where pilgrims bathe as part of the Gaya-style ancestral rites performed here.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"పురుహూతికా దేవి ఆలయం","morning_opens_at"