suru","town":"Talakadu","latitude":12.2,"longitude":77.0333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kaveri","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Feb–Mar (Panchalinga Darshana, held once every 12 years, is the biggest event); otherwise Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T18:27:49.795249+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Once the capital of the Western Ganga dynasty, and by tradition home to more than thirty temples now mostly buried under Kaveri riverside sand dunes. Local tradition attributes the burial to a curse laid by Queen Alamelamma of Srirangapatna in the 16th century, after Mysore's Wodeyar rulers seized her jewels — she is said to have drowned herself in the Kaveri, cursing the town to turn to sand; historians instead point to river-course shifts and wind-driven erosion. The Vaidyeshwara Temple is among the few structures still visible above the sand.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ವೈದ್ಯೇಶ್ವರ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ, ತಲಕಾಡು","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mysore Mandakalli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":41.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chamarajanagar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":31.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"6bfafe29-7ac2-43d1-b469-d1ac22027162","name":"Varinjam Sree Subramanya Swamy Temple","deity":"Murugan (Subramanya)","sampradaya":"Kaumara","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Kollam","town":"Karamcode","latitude":8.8525,"longitude":76.7394