 window here — like the rest of Tamil Nadu's coast and interior, Kumbakonam gets its main rain from the northeast monsoon in Oct–Nov, the opposite of most of India's calendar. The Mahamaham tank festival, held every 12 years, is the exception worth planning around regardless of season.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds that after a great deluge, Shiva, as a physician, gathered the scattered fragments of the nectar-pot (kumbha) of creation that had washed here, and shaped the temple's linga from the resulting sand — giving Kumbakonam (kumbha-koṇam) its name.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ஆதி கும்பேஸ்வரர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Thanjavur Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":39.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kumbakonam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"703c4c57-8742-498a-91f1-9ad4407f431d","name":"Bhalei Mata Temple","deity":"Bhadra Kali","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Himachal Pradesh","district":"Chamba","town":"Barangal","latitude":32.631,"longitude":76.007,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Baira River","river_distance_km":0.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple to the goddess Bhadra on a high spur at Bhalei, about 40 km from Chamba and 30 km from Dalhousie. The deity is a two-foot black stone image in the sanctum. It attracts many pilgrims, and a large havan is performed during the Navratras of Ashwin and Chaitra.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pathankot Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":56.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nurpur Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":41.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Bhalei Mata Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"7053f09c-00da-4403-a70d-c9e0cafe860d","name":"Navagraha Mandir, Guwahati","deity":"Navagraha (nine planetary deities)","sampradaya":"Smarta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Assam","district":"Kamrup Metropolitan","town":"Guwahati","latitude":26.19092,"longitude":91.76525,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Brahmaputra River","river_distance_km":1.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:09.085477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient temple on Chitrachal Hill in Guwahati. Its sanctum holds lingams for the nine celestial bodies of Vedic astrology: Surya, Chandra, Mangala, Rahu, Shani, Ketu, Brihaspati, Budha and Shukra. It is a notable site in Assam.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lokpriya Gopinath Bordoloi International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":20,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Guwahati railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Navagraha Mandir, Guwahati), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"7163a146-c21a-46cb-b832-50a6597bd814","name":"Jyotiba Temple, Kolhapur","deity":"Jyotiba (Brahma-Vishnu-Shiva combined)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Kolhapur","town":"Panhala","latitude":16.7833,"longitude":74.15,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kasari River","river_distance_km":3.1,"best_season_notes":"Mar–Apr for the Chaitra Yatra fair on Chaitra Purnima.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T18:27:49.795249+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Set on a hilltop in the Panhala range, with the current structure dating to 1730 under the Maratha noble Ranoji Shinde, replacing an earlier 17th-century shrine. Tradition holds the three gods Brahma, Vishnu, and Shiva combined into a single form, Jyotiba, specifically to destroy the demon Ratnasura and later the demon Raktabhoja, freeing the region from their oppression. The temple's Chaitra Yatra is known for its colourful processions and clouds of gulal (pink powder).","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ज्योतिबा मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Ratnagiri Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":91,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shri Chatrapati Shahu Maharaj Terminus railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":12.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":18},{"id":"72342acd-7cd8-496e-9ebe-dfe71e6bd2bc","name":"Bugga Ramalingeswara Swamy Temple","deity":"Shiva as Ramalingeswara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Anantapuramu","town":"Tadipatri","latitude":14.9184,"longitude":78.0101,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Penna","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple on the south bank of the Penna at Tadipatri, built between 1490 and 1509 by Pemmasani Ramalinga Nayudu I under Vijayanagara rule. The lingam is considered self-originated. Seven small pillars before the Vishnu shrine sound musical notes when struck, and the unfinished gopurams were praised by James Anderson.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sri Sathya Sai Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":88.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tadipatri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Bugga Ramalingeswara Swamy Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Vijayanagara","construction_century":15},{"id":"726ed74a-3a22-4d8f-a786-8db2221669e4","name":"Sri Santhana Venugopala Swamy Temple, Thettu","deity":"Vishnu as Santhana Venugopala Swamy","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Annamayya","town":"Kondavaripalle","latitude":14.0198,"longitude":78.7384,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mandavi River","river_distance_km":2.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old Vishnu temple in Thettu village, Annamayya district, where the deity is also called Bala Gopala. A twelve-day annual Brahmotsavam in March or April draws over 100,000 people, and Mukkoti Ekadasi is observed with fasting and vigils. A shrine to Paleti Gangamma is in the village.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kadapa Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":55.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kalikiri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":42.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Sri Santhana Venugopala Swamy Temple, Thettu), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"72cc75f4-eaea-4015-9153-31dca4ee1f66","name":"Thousand Pillar Temple, Hanamkonda","deity":"Shiva (Rudreshwara), with Vishnu and Surya co-enshrined in a triple shrine (Trikutalayam)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Kakatiya monument"],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Hanamkonda","town":"Hanamkonda","latitude":18.0037,"longitude":79.5747,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:36:33.433509+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built by order of the Kakatiya king Rudra Deva in the 12th century (a consecration year of 1163 CE is commonly cited, though the temple's own documented history gives a broader 12th–13th century range for the Kakatiya building programme here). Its star-shaped triple-shrine (Trikutalayam) plan houses Shiva, Vishnu and Surya together, and it is renowned for a monolithic dolerite Nandi and finely detailed stone carving. Damaged in later centuries, it was restored with a donation from the 7th Nizam of Hyderabad and again by the Government of India in 2004; it is now ASI-protected.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Warangal Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":10.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Warangal railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Temple inscriptions; Archaeological Survey of India records","architecture_style":"Kakatiya (Vesara / later Chalukyan), star-shaped triple-shrine plan","construction_century":12},{"id":"73122e52-2afc-441f-9397-395558d07a3e","name":"Sri Vedantha Desikar Devasthanam, Mylapore","deity":"Vedanta Desikar (Acharya)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Mylapore","latitude":13.0332,"longitude":80.2688,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":1.9,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb, or around the Vedanta Desika Jayanti (Panguni).","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"On the same street as the Adi Kesava Perumal temple, this devasthanam to the 13th–14th-century philosopher-saint Vedanta Desika is regarded as the city's foremost landmark of the Desika (Vadakalai) branch of Sri Vaishnavism.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":11.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thirumayilai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"733edcca-bbba-42d8-adda-e24f21af3ca5","name":"Ganpati Temple, Tasgaon","deity":"Ganesha","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Sangli","town":"Chinchani","latitude":17.03333,"longitude":74.66667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Agrani River","river_distance_km":10.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Ganesha temple in Tasgaon, Sangli district. Unlike most Ganesha images, whose trunk curves left, the idol here has a right-curving trunk, which is considered active or living and able to bless worshippers. The idol is decorated with solid gold weighing 125 kg.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Belgaum Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":130.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nandre railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":13.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ganpati Temple, Tasgaon), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"73addaed-1fce-4f7d-b522-0469ec7016f6","name":"Charbhuja Nath Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Charbhujanath","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Bundi","town":"Balchand Para","latitude":25.4459,"longitude":75.6373,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Manoli River","river_distance_km":8.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old east-facing temple in Bundi, Rajasthan, dedicated to Charbhujanath, a four-armed form of Vishnu. Large numbers of devotees come on Krishna Janmashtami, and a Phagotsav celebration has been held here around Holi for the last 500 years.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kota Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":38,"nearest_railway_s