approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple at Dharahara village near Raghopur in Supaul district, Bihar, also called Dharahara Mahadev Mandir. No firm evidence dates its founding, though tradition places it in the Mahabharata age. It was renovated in the 20th century and is busiest at Maha Shivaratri, Shravan, Naga Panchami and Kartik Purnima.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Purnea Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":79.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Raghopur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Bhimshankar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"77e0d501-14b2-4b3a-96f5-cac397bd6f86","name":"Varadavinayak Temple, Mahad","deity":"Varadavinayak (Ganesha)","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":["Ashtavinayak"],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Raigad","town":"Mahad (near Khopoli)","latitude":18.7667,"longitude":73.4167,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Savitri River","river_distance_km":0,"best_season_notes":"Ganesh Chaturthi (Aug–Sep) is the busiest day; Oct–Feb otherwise for the Ashtavinayak circuit.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:05:55.016033+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:12:14.428399+00:00","sthala_purana":"The Varadvinayak idol is said to have been found immersed in the adjoining lake around 1690 CE; the temple and the town of Mahad were built around it by Ramji Mahadev Biwalkar, a Kalyan subhedar, in 1725 (some sources credit Ranoji Shinde instead).","etiquette_notes":"The only Ashtavinayak temple where devotees may approach and personally touch the idol, rather than viewing it from a distance.","native_name":"श्री वरदविनायक मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mumbai (Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International) or Pune Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":null,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karjat or Khopoli railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"maharashtratourism.gov.in (Ashtavinayak, Mahad)","architecture_style":"A small shrine (about 8 ft square) with a gold-plated dome around 25 ft high, ringed by carved elephant statues — Peshwa-period Maratha temple style","construction_century":18},{"id":"78363171-dcc8-4b5a-9c4e-dd05e1ecbb8c","name":"Ettumanoor Mahadeva Temple","deity":"Mahadeva (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Kottayam","town":"Ettumanoor","latitude":9.6833,"longitude":76.55,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Meenachil River","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Feb–Mar around the temple's Arattu festival; otherwise Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:20:34.20482+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T11:30:32.947142+00:00","sthala_purana":"Local tradition associates the temple with worship by the Pandavas and the sage Vyasa. The present structure, including its fortifications, was rebuilt in 717 ME (1542 CE).","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ഏറ്റുമാനൂർ മഹാദേവക്ഷേത്രം","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"4am–12pm and 5pm–8pm, per a moderate-authority source — not confirmed against the Devaswom board's own listing.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport (Nedumbassery)","nearest_airport_distance_km":75,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ettumanoor railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ettumanoor Mahadevar Temple)","architecture_style":"Traditional Kerala temple architecture: a copper-tiled circular sanctum with 14 ornamental finials, a golden dwajasthambham, carved woodwork and Dravidian-influenced mural paintings — including the \"Pradosha Nritham\" (Shiva's dance) fresco, regarded as one of India's finest temple murals","construction_century":16},{"id":"7869a2cc-32f9-42f6-835a-f3ed7712e43e","name":"Mata Kaushalya Temple","deity":"Kaushalya, mother of Rama","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Chhattisgarh","district":"Raipur","town":"Arang Tahsil","latitude":21.3194,"longitude":81.8131,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kulhan River","river_distance_km":1.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Located at Chandkhuri village, about 27 km from Raipur, this temple honours Mata Kaushalya, mother of Rama, and is described as the only one dedicated to her. In 2020 the state's chief minister laid the foundation stone for its expansion, with the stated aim of keeping its original form intact.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Swami Vivekananda Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":16.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mandir Hasaud railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Mata Kaushalya Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"78ab9912-c633-4542-9d3b-7b14932ec14b","name":"Kudroli Gokarnanatheshwara Temple","deity":"Gokarnanatheshwara (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Dakshina Kannada","town":"Mangaluru","latitude":12.8833,"longitude":74.8333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Anna Dhana — free vegetarian meals, a tradition since the temple's founding in 1912, with especially large-scale service during Navaratri","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0,"nearest_river_name":"Gurupura River","river_distance_km":1.2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; the temple's Navarathri Deepotsava (lamp festival) is a major draw.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:30:52.99453+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Founded in 1912 by the social reformer Narayana Guru, who by tradition envisioned the temple in a dream, at a time when many communities were denied entry to existing temples. Guru's teaching — \"one caste, one religion, one God for all mankind\" — shaped this and roughly a hundred other temples he founded across Kerala and coastal Karnataka to be open to every devotee regardless of caste. The deity, Shiva as Gokarnanatha, shares his form with the older pilgrimage site of Gokarna.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಕುದ್ರೋಳಿ ಗೋಕರ್ಣನಾಥೇಶ್ವರ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mangalore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":9.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mangaluru Central railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":20},{"id":"78f362e4-d370-4aad-87d6-31de556b83c9","name":"Kartikeya Temple, Pehowa","deity":"Kartikeya","sampradaya":"Kaumara","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Haryana","district":"Kurukshetra","town":"Pehowa","latitude":29.98,"longitude":76.58,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Markanda River","river_distance_km":9.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple at Pehowa in Haryana, called one of the oldest Kartikeya temples in North India. Kartikeya is also known as Murugan, Skanda and Shanmukha. The article notes early veneration of Skanda by the Kushanas, Yaudheyas, Ikshvakus and Guptas, who issued coins bearing his image.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sarsawa Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":79.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Pehowa Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.4,"emergency_contact_