icated to the goddess Ugratara. Tradition links it to the navel of Sati. The sanctum holds no image; a small water-filled pit is revered as the goddess. The present temple was built by Ahom king Siva Singha in 1725, beside the Jorepukhuri tank, with a Shiva shrine nearby.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lokpriya Gopinath Bordoloi International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":18.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Guwahati railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ugratara Devalaya), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":18},{"id":"7972fb39-776d-46bd-a901-ece88608f695","name":"Gudem Gutta Shree Satyanarayana Swamy Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Satyanarayana Swamy","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Mancherial","town":"Kamepalle","latitude":18.9059,"longitude":79.17228,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Godavari","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A hilltop temple in Gudem village, Mancherial district, on the bank of the Godavari. It honours Vishnu as Satyanarayana Swamy and is nicknamed Telangana's Annavaram after the well-known Satyanarayana temple in Andhra Pradesh. It is regarded as one of the best-known temples in Telangana.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Ramagundam Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":32.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Peddampet railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":29.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Gudem Gutta Shree Satyanarayana Swamy Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"797b61ce-7d25-4331-b51f-8b49d94c4a5d","name":"Sri Krishna Matha, Udupi","deity":"Krishna","sampradaya":"Madhwa","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Udupi","town":"Udupi","latitude":13.341,"longitude":74.7457,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"Madhwa Sarovar tank within the Matha complex is used for daily Sandhya Vandanam by pilgrims and students.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"yes","samidhadhanam_notes":"Ashta Matha kitchens can arrange samidha on request a day in advance — ask at the Paryaya Matha office.","food_tier":"brahmin_run_kitchen","food_source_name":"Sri Krishna Matha Bhojana Shala","food_source_contact":"+91-820-252-0225","food_distance_km":0,"nearest_river_name":"Indrani River","river_distance_km":4,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb is coolest; Paryaya festival years (every two years, in January) draw large crowds. Udupi's coast gets very heavy southwest-monsoon rain June–September, more than inland Karnataka.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T18:43:32.800302+00:00","sthala_purana":"The image of Krishna here is said to have been given by Rukmini and recovered by Madhvacharya from a ship's cargo of gopichandana, the vessel saved from a storm by his intervention. The deity faces west and is worshipped through a nine-holed window, the Navagraha Kindi, which by tradition was opened for the devotee Kanakadasa, refused entry at the door.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಶ್ರೀ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಮಠ","morning_opens_at":"04:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:00:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"21:00:00","timings_notes":"Closed roughly 1–3pm for rituals and puja preparation.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mangalore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":100,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Udupi Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"79968683-4884-40d3-8309-6befe8ac93e6","name":"Gangeshwar Asthan","deity":"Shiva as Gangeshwar Nath (lingam)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Darbhanga","town":"Jale","latitude":26.29099,"longitude":85.7194,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Budhnagra-Samri Nadi River","river_distance_km":1.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:24.13334+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple in Darbhanga, Bihar, where Shiva is worshipped in lingam form and which has been a religious site for centuries. It is managed under the Baba Gangeshwarnath Tirth Chetra.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Darbhanga Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":22.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kamtaul railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":10.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Gangeshwar Asthan), summarised; location 