pen roughly May–June and Sept–Nov; closed and inaccessible under snow in winter, when its deity is moved down to Mukunath near Chopta.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T08:35:20.91066+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"The third and highest of the five Panch Kedar temples, at 3,680 m — among the highest Shiva temples in the world, just below the Chandrashila peak. Tradition holds that after the Mahabharata war, Shiva evaded the Pandavas seeking absolution by taking the form of a bull and diving into the ground; where his body reappeared in five pieces became the five Panch Kedar shrines, and his arms (bahu) are said to have surfaced here. Local tradition credits the temple's founding to Arjuna, and later Adi Shankaracharya, though it is thought to be over a thousand years old.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"तुंगनाथ मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":104.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"North Indian Himalayan (Katyuri)","construction_century":null},{"id":"7ccaf1c0-ce9d-4e6a-94de-de891540d387","name":"Bhavatarini Shmashanpith Kali Temple","deity":"Bhavatarini Kali","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Purba Medinipur","town":"Panskura","latitude":22.39417,"longitude":87.71565,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kangsabati River","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"s