mple at Santhoor near Padubidri, Karnataka, where Kartikeya is worshipped as Subramanya, lord of serpents. Festivals include Shashti, Kiru Shashti and Nagara Panchami. During the Shashti Mahotsav, thousands of devotees arrive early in the morning for darshan and special offerings.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mangalore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":23.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nandikoor railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Santhoor Subramanya Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"7fc6e4f0-f7f2-4703-bba7-55523bf9b3ce","name":"Radha Rani Temple","deity":"Radha Krishna (Laadli Lal)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Mathura","town":"Chiksoli","latitude":27.65028,"longitude":77.37361,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"A historic temple on the Bhanugarh hill, about 250 metres high, at Barsana in Mathura district. It is dedicated to Radha, and Radha and Krishna are worshipped together here as Laadli Lal. It draws large crowds, especially for Radhashtami and Lathmar Holi.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Noida International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":62.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chata railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":14.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Radha Rani Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"7fdb43dc-10ec-43cc-866b-ed25721f000f","name":"Swaminarayan Mandir, Gadhada","deity":"Radha Krishna (Gopinathji)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Botad","town":"Gadhada","latitude":21.96663,"longitude":71.57483,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kalubhar River","river_distance_km":13.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:27.898205+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in Gadhada, Gujarat, also called Gopinathji Dev Mandir, belonging to the Swaminarayan Sampradaya. It is one of six temples built by the founder of the sect, Swaminarayan, and is dedicated to Radha Krishna.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Bhavnagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":67.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Alampur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":14.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Swaminarayan Mandir, Gadhada), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"81389edf-eb98-4be9-8d6e-a91bce59ddc1","name":"Shantadurga Temple, Kavalem","deity":"Shantadurga (Parvati)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Goa","district":"Ponda","town":"Kavalem","latitude":15.4167,"longitude":74.0667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khandepar River","river_distance_km":0.4,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb, cool and dry season away from Goa's monsoon.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds Parvati took this form to make peace between Vishnu and Shiva when they came to blows — Shanta-durga, \"the goddess who pacifies\". The deity was moved inland to Kavalem from Old Goa during the Portuguese era to protect it from destruction.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"शांतादुर्गा मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Goa International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":25.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chandar Goa railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":17,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"813e8765-ee51-48a4-a2a6-84d332d85245","name":"Meenakshi Amman Temple, Madurai","deity":"Meenakshi (Parvati) & Sundareswarar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha","Pancha Sabhai"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Madurai","town":"Madurai","latitude":9.9195,"longitude":78.1193,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple Annaprasadam Hall — free meals since 2002","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.1,"nearest_river_name":"Vaigai","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Mar is most reliable; the Meenakshi Thirukalyanam festival (Apr/May) draws enormous crowds and real heat. Madurai, like the rest of Tamil Nadu, gets its main rain from the northeast monsoon in Oct–Nov.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T06:23:03.123234+00:00","sthala_purana":"Meenakshi was born to the Pandya king Malayadhwaja with three breasts, and it was foretold that the third would vanish when she met the one she was to marry — which happened when she encountered Shiva as Sundareswarar. Their marriage, the Thirukalyanam, is re-enacted each year as the temple's great festival.","etiquette_notes":"Modest dress is expected; some sanctum areas restrict shorts and sleeveless tops. Non-Hindus are generally welcomed here, unlike some of the stricter Kerala and Odisha temples in this directory.","native_name":"மீனாட்சி அம்மன் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":"05:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:30:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"21:30:00","timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":12,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Madurai Junction","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":14},{"id":"819d3d75-98c4-4a70-b427-784a72b5ba04","name":"Mahanandeeswara Swamy Temple, Mahanandi","deity":"Shiva (Mahanandeeswara)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Nava Nandi"],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Nandyal","town":"Mahanandi","latitude":15.47056,"longitude":78.62611,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Pala Eru River","river_distance_km":2.4,"best_season_notes":"Maha Shivaratri (Feb–Mar) is the major festival here.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:36:33.433509+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient shrine, traditionally said to be over 1,500 years old, with its gopuram attributed to the Badami Chalukyas (7th century) and further additions under Vijayanagara patronage in the 10th–15th centuries. One of the \"Nava Nandi\" cluster of nine Nandi/Shiva shrines within about 15 km of each other, Mahanandi is known above all for its perennial spring-fed square tanks (pushkarinis, traditionally named for Brahma, Vishnu and Rudra), whose water is considered never to run dry.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":56.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Gazulapalle railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local tradition; Nava Nandi cluster history","architecture_style":"Dravidian; Badami Chalukyan-style gopuram with Vijayanagara-era additions","construction_century":7},{"id":"81c07a27-af2d-4a5a-84d5-c1439ac5343a","name":"Ganesha Temple, Morgaon","deity":"Ganesha as Mayureshwar (Moreshwar)","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Pune","town":"Morgaon","latitude":18.27606,"longitude":74.32139,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Karha River","river_distance_km":0.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Ganesha temple at Morgaon, about 65 km from Pune, where the Ashtavinayaka pilgrimage begins and ends. It is the foremost centre of the Ganapatya sect. According to tradition Ganesha killed the demon Sindhura here. The temple's date is unknown; it prospered under Peshwa patronage and the descendants of Moraya Gosavi.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pune International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":54.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Jejuri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":15.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ganesha Temple, Morgaon), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"81cee881-8616-4386-9922-b3fb616a3601","name":"Aadhipureeswarar Temple, Tiruvottiyur","deity":"Aadhipureeswarar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Tiruvottiyur","latitude":13.1608,"longitude":80.301,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bay of Bengal","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Reported to be 1,000–2,000 years old, one of the Padal Petra Sthalams glorified in the Tevaram hymns of the Nayanmar saints, paired with the adjacent Vadivudai Amman shrine.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":23.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruvottiyur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey; Tevaram","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"81f19679-a5e4-4155-8d8d-3840aa497386","name":"Khatu Shyam Ji Temple","deity":"Khatu Shyam (Barbarika)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Sikar","town":"Khatu","latitude":27.6167,"longitude":75.15,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Daily bhandara — free vegetarian meals organized by devotees and the temple, with larger bhandaras during Phalgun and the Chaitra/Ashvin Purnima fairs","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Feb–Mar, around the Falgun Mela, is the busiest and most festive time.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T18:23:31.36475+00:00","sthala_purana":"Dedicated to Barbarika, grandson of Bhima, who according to the Mahabharata offered to fight on the losing side out of a vow of fairness. Krishna, testing him, asked for his head as charity before the war; Barbarika's severed head watched the battle from a hilltop and was later granted the boon of being worshipped as Krishna's own form, Khatu Shyam, in the Kali Yuga.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"खाटू श्याम जी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":"05:30:00","morning_closes_at":"13:00:00","evening_opens_at":"17:00:00","evening_closes_at":"21:00:00","timings_notes":"Summer hours run roughly an hour either side (4:30am–12:30pm, 4–10pm); open 24 hours during Ekadashi and the Phalgun Mela.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaipur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":265,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khatu Shyam Road Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition, not a single classical Sanskrit text","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"82632dc9-7794-4958-a287-81af8a31a997","name":"Koulutla Chennakesava Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Chennakesava","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Kurnool","town":"Timmapuram","latitude":15.85639,"longitude":77.37694,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Suguru Vanka River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"This temple lies in a reserved forest at Kappatralla in Devanakonda mandal, about 50 km from Kurnool. The Vijayanagara king Krishnadevaraya is said to have built the complex. It also includes Shiva shrines, among them Mallikarjuna Swamy with Bramarambika, Vijaya Vinayaka, Dakshinamurthy and Viswanatha.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":86.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Iranagallu railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":12.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Koulutla Chennakesava Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"82900795-deb6-4bbe-99b5-1be41d4f3002","name":"Renuka Devi Temple, Mahur","deity":"Renuka / Ekaveerika (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Nanded","town":"Mahur","latitude":19.8326,"longitude":77.9233,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Penganga","river_distance_km":2.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; the hillock climb is best avoided in peak summer or monsoon.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:10:03.827717+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Set on a hillock above Mahur, this is one of Maharashtra's most revered Devi shrines. Puranic tradition holds that Renuka, wife of the sage Jamadagni and mother of Parashurama, was beheaded by her own son on his father's command and her head fell here — hence the temple's Renuka identity. Adi Shankaracharya's Ashtadasha Shakti Peetha Stotram separately names Mahur as the seat of Ekaveerika, where Sati's right hand is said to have fallen; the two traditions are worshipped together at this one site, with no image but a vermilion-smeared stone (tandla) as the murti. Mahur is also revered as the birthplace of Dattatreya.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"रेणुका देवी मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Shri Guru Gobind Singh Ji Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":95.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ambari(Deccan) railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":34.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Puranic tradition (Renuka/Parashurama legend) and the Ashtadasha Shakti Peetha Stotram","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"8331fa5c-42d4-4a71-86ae-5b70a27df9b2","name":"Avanibhajana Pallaveshwaram Temple","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvannamalai","town":"Vandavasi","latitude":12.43111,"longitude":79.46639,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Tondiaru River","river_distance_km":10.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:59.708182+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A rock-cut Shiva temple at Seeyamangalam, Tiruvannamalai district, Tamil Nadu, made under the Pallava king Mahendravarman I in the 7th century CE, with later Chola and Vijayanagar additions. A pillar carries a Nataraja sculpture thought to be the earliest of its kind in South India. It is a protected monument under the Archaeological Survey of India.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Puducherry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":63.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tindivanam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":30.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Avanibhajana Pallaveshwaram Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Rock-cut","construction_century":7},{"id":"836cc78f-a20c-41e0-ac53-ece684b22c9f","name":"Nand Temple, Nandaprayag","deity":"Vishnu","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Panch Prayag"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Chamoli","town":"Nandaprayag","latitude":30.33,"longitude":79.33,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Alaknanda–Nandakini confluence","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Mar–Jun and Sep–Nov.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:22:57.994564+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"The second of the Panch Prayag, where the Alaknanda meets the Nandakini river. Once the capital of a local Yadu kingdom, the site takes its name from King Nanda — the foster father of Krishna in the Bhagavata tradition — who is said to have performed intense penance here on a sacred stone, seeking a son from Vishnu; the temple is traditionally held to stand on that very stone.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"नंद मंदिर, नंदप्रयाग","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":111.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"839e2989-850c-47a2-a237-a4cf40e9c781","name":"Yadagirigutta Lakshmi Narasimha Temple","deity":"Lakshmi Narasimha","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Yadadri Bhuvanagiri","town":"Yadagirigutta","latitude":17.5833,"longitude":78.9463,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Annaprasadam hall serving roughly 500 devotees daily free of charge, alongside daily distribution of Pulihora and Daddojanam prasadam","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0,"nearest_river_name":"Cholleru Vagu River","river_distance_km":6.6,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb, after Telangana's southwest monsoon (Jun–Sep) has fully cleared; the hill shrine was fully renovated in recent years with a new granite temple complex, so facilities hold up well even in the cooler crowds of Brahmotsavam season.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Named for the sage Yadarishi, who is said to have performed penance here seeking a vision of Narasimha in every one of his forms at once. Tradition holds the deity appeared in five aspects together in a hill cave — Jwala, Gandabherunda, Yogananda, Ugra, and Lakshmi Narasimha.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"యాదగిరిగుట్ట లక్ష్మీ నరసింహ స్వామి ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Begumpet Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":52.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Yadadri (Raigir) railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Dravidian, modeled on Kakatiya-era temple architecture; the roughly thousand-year-old shrine was entirely rebuilt (2016–2022) in black granite (Krishnashila) without cement, concrete, or bricks","construction_century":21},{"id":"83d14fec-c66f-42c2-8f64-bf34b8ace9ca","name":"Kalaram Temple","deity":"Rama as Kalaram","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Nashik","town":"Nashik","latitude":20.00694,"longitude":73.7955,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Waghadi River","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Rama temple in the Panchavati area of Nashik, Maharashtra. Its name comes from the black statue of Rama, kalaram meaning black Rama. The sanctum also houses Sita and Lakshmana, and thousands of devotees visit daily.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Nashik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":15.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nashik Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kalaram Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"83e55eb5-03b5-4dd5-b3de-ebdd5d6f068e","name":"Shri Mansa Mata Mandir Hasampur","deity":"Mansa Devi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Sikar","town":"Hasampur","latitude":27.76331,"longitude":76.02325,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Sota River","river_distance_km":10.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple of Mansa Devi at Hasampur in Sikar district, spread over about 100 acres at the foot of the Hasampur hills near Neem-Ka-Thana. It is counted among the prominent Shakti temples of North India. Thousands of devotees visit, with numbers rising to lakhs daily during the nine-day Navratra fair.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaipur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":105.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dabla railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":15.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Mansa Mata Mandir Hasampur), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"83f2931e-05db-4675-9456-02128bde2c04","name":"Sekhareswar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Sekhareswar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Jagatsinghapur","town":"Tirtol","latitude":20.27143,"longitude":86.43578,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mahanadi River","river_distance_km":6.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:38.196668+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple in Lathanga village, Jagatsinghpur district, Odisha. The text says its Varuni Yatra has been held for a thousand years. A Sanskrit tol, a Sanskrit college and a youth group are named after the deity, and a board of trustees looks after the temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":65,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rahama railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Sekhareswar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"841c5ad3-bbd9-43ec-ae7c-050dd3926b74","name":"Chandi Devi Temple, Haridwar","deity":"Chandi Devi (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Sapta Puri"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Haridwar","town":"Haridwar","latitude":29.9709,"longitude":78.1972,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"Atop Neel Parvat overlooking the Ganga; Har Ki Pauri ghat below is the main ritual-bathing spot in town.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganga","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar; extremely crowded during Kumbh/Ardh Kumbh Mela years.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition credits Adi Shankaracharya with installing the deity here on the banks of the Ganga at Haridwar. The temple, reached by a ropeway or a hillside climb, is dedicated to Chandi, the form of Devi described in the Devi Mahatmyam as having slain the demon generals Chanda and Munda — from which both the goddess's epithet and the hill's name are said to derive.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"चंडी देवी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":"A hilltop temple; a ropeway (Aarti Udankhatola) covers most of the climb for those who cannot walk it, alongside the traditional stepped path.","nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":24.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Motichur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"84329153-f576-482d-8d0b-c3f1fdef40da","name":"Vaitheeswaran Koil","deity":"Vaitheeswaran (Shiva) / Thaiyal Nayagi","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Navagraha Sthalam"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Mayiladuthurai","town":"Vaitheeswaran Koil","latitude":11.15,"longitude":79.6667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cauvery River","river_distance_km":4.6,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; Tuesdays, associated with the planet Mars, are considered especially auspicious here.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:30:52.99453+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built roughly a thousand years ago and revered as a Paadal Petra Sthalam, sung by the 7th-century Nayanar saints. Shiva is worshipped here as Vaitheeswaran, \"the healing god,\" with Parvati as Thaiyal Nayagi, \"the mother who stitches wounds.\" Tradition holds this is where the planet Mars (Angaraka), afflicted with leprosy, was cured by the deity — making the temple one of the nine Navagraha shrines of Tamil Nadu, specifically associated with Mars. The temple is also closely tied to Nadi astrology, palm-leaf readings said to have been recorded here by ancient sages.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"வைத்தீஸ்வரன் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Neyveli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":53.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Anandtandavpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"844a2d23-53e7-4af8-918b-1a73aba3bcfd","name":"Sharadhamba Temple, West Mambalam","deity":"Sharadhamba (Saraswati)","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"West Mambalam","latitude":13.0355,"longitude":80.2185,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":1.4,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Nov, around Navaratri/Vasant Panchami.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Saraswati shrine on Kripa Shankari Street, West Mambalam, distinct from the similarly named Sharadhamba temple a short walk away on Venkatanarayana Road, T. Nagar.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":7.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mambalam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"855117a3-77ef-4875-97b5-63a524ed9ab5","name":"Maa Ugra Tara","deity":"Ugratara (Tara)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Tangi","latitude":19.95843,"longitude":85.46835,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mandagini River","river_distance_km":8.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Ugratara was the tutelary goddess of the Eastern Ganga kings, and her old temple is at Mulajharigarh village near Bhusandapur. She is shown three-eyed and four-armed, standing on a corpse above a pyre. She is one of the ten Mahavidyas, worshipped in tantric fashion. Chaitra Parba and Sharadiya Durga Puja are main festivals.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":48.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhusandpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Maa Ugra Tara), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"85d1b5cb-b01b-4afb-8a36-f33028c3b5c3","name":"Tungareshwar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Tungareshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Palghar","town":"Ambawadi","latitude":19.4165,"longitude":72.9015,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Sopara Creek River","river_distance_km":6.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:14.599574+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple on the Tungareshwar plateau near Vasai in Palghar district, with a Ram Kund behind it and a small shrine of Khodiyaar Mataji nearby. Devotees come for Maha Shivratri and Khodiyar Jayanti, and a bhandara feast is held on Mondays of Shravan.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Open 5 am to 6 pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":36.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Juichandra railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Tungareshwar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"85e26a85-dd78-4cef-99e1-128ad1e83884","name":"Devipuram","deity":"Sahasrakshi (Lalita Tripurasundari) with Kameshwara","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Anakapalli","town":"Pallavanipalem","latitude":17.76537,"longitude":83.08296,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Meghadri Gedda River","river_distance_km":10.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:27.898205+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple complex near Visakhapatnam in Andhra Pradesh, belonging mainly to the Shakta tradition. It is dedicated to the goddess Sahasrakshi, understood as a form of Lalita Tripurasundari or Parvati, together with her consort Kameshwara, a form of Shiva.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Alluri Sitarama Raju International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":50.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thadi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Devipuram), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"86286b72-f316-4a92-a863-2ffc2cd0d65a","name":"Penchalakona Lakshmi Narasimha Swamy Temple","deity":"Lakshmi Narasimha, worshipped as Swayambhu (self-manifested); also called Penusila Lakshmi Narasimha","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Nellore","town":"Penchalakona","latitude":14.3365,"longitude":79.4104,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Annadanam offered by the Devasthanam (reported by a recent visitor; not officially confirmed)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0,"nearest_river_name":"Kalleru River","river_distance_km":12.2,"best_season_notes":"The five-day Brahmotsavam begins on Vaisakha Shuddha Ekadashi (April–May); Narasimha Jayanti is also observed.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:40:38.920003+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"After slaying Hiranyakashipu, Narasimha could not calm his anger and wandered the forest. Lakshmi came as the Chenchu tribal woman Chenchu Lakshmi and embraced him; the embrace (penu vesukonuta) and the rock (sila) give the name Penusila, later Penchalakona. Sources differ in detail — one says the Lord married Chenchu Lakshmi, the daughter of the Chenchu chief, and turned to rock; others say she simply embraced and calmed him — so this is recorded as tradition, not history. The place is also linked to the sage Kanva's penance. The temple is said to date from the Krita yuga, a mythic claim; no date for the present structure was found. Coordinates are approximate.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per the Nellore district tourism site, not the temple's own schedule: roughly 6:30am–12:30pm and 3–7:30pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati (Renigunta) Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":null,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rapuru railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":19.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Nellore district administration site; Wikipedia (Penchalakona)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"863708b8-84bd-4281-a57a-2dbae3bf2d23","name":"Ashtabhujakaram, Kanchipuram","deity":"Ashta Bhuja Perumal (eight-armed Vishnu) / Alamelumangai","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Kanchipuram","town":"Kanchipuram","latitude":12.8225,"longitude":79.71083,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vegavathy","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-09T13:54:39.898029+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the 108 Divya Desams and the fourth-largest temple in southern Kanchipuram, believed to have been renovated by the later Pallavas. Vishnu is worshipped here in his eight-armed (ashta bhuja) form.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":53,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kanchipuram East railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Nalayira Divya Prabandham; local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian, Pallava origins","construction_century":null},{"id":"863ed679-c2e2-4063-92bc-9398c481979f","name":"Bhojeshwar Temple, Bhojpur","deity":"Shiva (a monolithic 7.5-foot / 2.3m lingam)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Unfinished temple","ASI Monument of National Importance"],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Raisen","town":"Bhojpur","latitude":23.1003,"longitude":77.5797,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Betwa River","river_distance_km":0.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:07:42.20596+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Construction began in the 11th century (around 1035 CE, per inscription and sculpture dating) under the Paramara king Bhoja, and was left unfinished for reasons that aren't documented. Over 1,300 architectural plans and mason's marks are still engraved on the rocks surrounding the site — a well-studied archaeological detail. One scholarly hypothesis (art historian Shri Krishna Deva) suggests the temple may have been intended as a funerary or memorial structure for Bhoja's father Sindhuraja or uncle Munja; this is a proposed reading, not a settled fact.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Approximately 6am–7pm per travel sources; some list it closed on Mondays, others say open daily — not confirmed by an official schedule.","accessibility_notes":"Received a 2015 National Tourism Award for disability accessibility.","nearest_airport_name":"Raja Bhoj International Airport, Bhopal","nearest_airport_distance_km":43.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Habibganj Railway Station, Bhopal","nearest_railway_distance_km":22.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Temple inscriptions and sculpture dating; art-historical scholarship (Shri Krishna Deva)","architecture_style":"11th-century; a 115×82×13-ft platform, four octagonal pillars roughly 40ft each, windowless sandstone walls, and a pyramidal roof that was planned but never completed","construction_century":11},{"id":"869594ab-bef5-47b2-9a43-c8b01652e31f","name":"Mahalakshmi Temple, Dahanu","deity":"Mahalakshmi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Palghar","town":"Charoti","latitude":19.94073,"longitude":72.93453,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Suseri River","river_distance_km":3.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Mahalakshmi temple beside the Mumbai-Ahmedabad highway in Dahanu taluka, said to have been founded in 1306 by a Koli king of Jawhar. The Jawhar ruler's flag is offered during worship. Management and ritual duties traditionally lie with the Satav clan of the Malhar Koli community, who treat her as clan goddess.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Daman Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":55.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vangaon railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":19,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Mahalakshmi Temple, Dahanu), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":14},{"id":"869c1d26-961d-4f00-bf6d-802a4a37d1c0","name":"Puliyur Mahavishnu Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Mayapiran (Thripuliyoorappan)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Alappuzha","town":"Puliyoor","latitude":9.30194,"longitude":76.58583,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Pamba River","river_distance_km":2.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Divya Desam in Alappuzha district, in Kerala style. Tradition says Bhima built it, as one of five ancient shrines near Chengannur linked to the Pandavas. The Aratu festival and Kavadiattam are its main celebrations. Travancore Devaswom Board administers it.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Stated hours: 4 am to 11 am and 5 pm to 8 pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"ne